{
  "name": "Delta Loop",
  "icon": "radiocraft:balun_four_to_one",
  "category": "radiocraft:antennas",
  "sortnum": 10,
  "pages": [
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "A $(thing)delta loop$() is a triangle of antenna wire one wavelength round, fed at a corner through a $(item)4:1 balun$(). It is the long-distance loop: weak up close (a tenth of the usual line of sight) and strong on skip (half as much again).$(br2)On 20 m: about 21 blocks round, each side about 7."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "title": "Building it",
      "text": "Wire from the balun to two corner holders, and a third wire between them: a closed triangle. Upright, flat or sloping all work. Keep the sides even: a lopsided triangle matches worse.$(br2)Hang it at least $(thing)4 blocks$() above the ground. Lower, it still works, but the SWR is a little worse and most of its skip is gone."
    },
